# Markdown standards

This repo uses **markdownlint** (see `.markdownlint.json`). Follow these rules on every edit so Problem badges stay at zero.

## Required on every markdown file

### First line is a level-1 heading (MD041)

The first line must be `# Title`.

### Fenced code blocks need a language (MD040)

Use `bash`, `text`, `typescript`, `sql`, etc. Never bare ` ``` ` alone.

### Tables use aligned style (MD060)

Example:

| Column one | Column two    |
| ---------- | ------------- |
| Value      | Another value |

Not compact `|a|b|` or `|----------|` without spaces.

### Line length ≤ 120 characters (MD013)

Wrap prose; break long URLs onto their own line if needed.

## Long content exceptions

For files where wrapping ruins readability (e.g. long audit metadata examples in
`docs/audit-logs.md`), add at the top after the H1:

```markdown
<!-- markdownlint-disable MD013 -->
```

Do not disable other rules unless documented in this file.

## After editing markdown

Run:

```bash
npm run lint:md
```

Fix all reported errors before considering the task done.

Build artifacts (`.next/`) and `node_modules/` are excluded via `.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc` and
`.vscode/settings.json` — do not lint those paths.

## Links and lists

- Use full URLs in links — no shortened paths
- One blank line before and after headings and fenced blocks
- No HTML entities in place of real characters (`&amp;` → `&`)
